    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n58991" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κοπρ-ίας</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ου</span>, ὁ, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κόπρος</span>) in pl.,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>buffoons</i>, a word first
			used under the Roman emperors, <i><span class="en">
				D.C.
				50.28
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				73.6
			</span></i>: Lat. <i>copreae</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Suet.
				<u>Tib.</u>
				61
			</span></i>. (Perh. so called because <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐκ κοπρίας
				ἀναιρεθέντες</span>, or because of their
		obscenity.)</div>
